# Line endings, pinned - because they reached the binary.
#
# With no .gitattributes and core.autocrlf=true, the same commit checked out
# twice produced different bytes: this working copy carried LF, a fresh clone
# carried CRLF, and Contract.cs alone differed by 658 bytes. The compiled
# assemblies differed too, which is why a build from a clean clone never matched
# the deployed one and the acceptance report had to record the difference as
# unexplained.
#
# What it did NOT break, measured rather than assumed: the contract hash is the
# same from either checkout (978fada188182306705ccb96 from both). Schemas are
# canonicalised with Formatting.None and every Description literal is a single
# line, so no newline reaches the hash. A server and an add-in built from
# differently-normalised checkouts still agree with each other.
#
# eol=lf, not eol=crlf: the repository is the source of truth and it is already
# LF. Windows tooling reads LF; Notepad has since Windows 10.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary, never touched.
*.rfa  binary
*.rvt  binary
*.rte  binary
*.png  binary
*.ico  binary
*.dll  binary
*.exe  binary
*.pdb  binary
*.zip  binary
